CHAPTER IV
RIGHTS OF VICTIMS
Article 5
(1) Every woman and child victim of violence has the right to: a. obtain protection for personal security, family, and property, and be free from threats related to testimony that will be, is being, or has been given;
b. participate in the process of selecting and determining the form of protection and security support;
c. be free from ensnaring questions;
d. obtain information regarding case developments and court decisions;
e. receive services that are fast, appropriate, comfortable, and according to needs;
f. obtain recovery, social reintegration, continuous handling up to rehabilitation and empowerment;
g. obtain assistance at every level of examination and during the judicial process and out-of-court processes are carried out; and
h. obtain psychological assistance, spiritual guidance, economic, social and interpreter services;
(2) The rights of victims as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.
Article 6 In addition to the rights as referred to in Article 5, every victim must: a. provide true information to the parties -9- concerned;
b. become a witness if it does not endanger oneself and if there is a security guarantee for the victim

Article 3
and child victims Protection of women and child victims of violence aims to: a. prevent all forms of violence against women and children, which occur within the household and/or community;
b. protect and provide a sense of security for women and children; c. provide legal assistance;
d. provide services to women and children -8- victims of violence, reporters and witnesses;
e. endeavor for recovery and social reintegration; and
f. increase community participation.

BENGKAYANG REGENCY GOVERNMENT
YEAR 2016
REGENT OF BENGKAYANG
WEST KALIMANTAN PROVINCE
REGIONAL REGULATION OF BENGKAYANG REGENCY
NUMBER 4 YEAR 2016
CONCERNING
THE IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION FOR WOMEN AND CHILDREN
VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE
BY THE GRACE OF GOD ALMIGHTY
THE REGENT OF BENGKAYANG,
Considering : a. that within every human being are inherent human rights that must be respected, upheld and protected by the state, law, Regional Government and every person for the sake of honor and protection of human dignity and worth;
b. that in reality the number of children in Bengkayang Regency exceeds one third of the population, so that the Regional Government is obligated to provide protection to children from all forms of violence, discrimination and exploitation, in order to ensure a decent and dignified livelihood and life for the children of Bengkayang Regency;
c. that children's issues must be handled comprehensively, in an integrated, directed and sustainable manner, thus requiring institutional support through legislation to support Bengkayang as a Child-Friendly Regency;
d. that based on Law Number 23 Year 2002 concerning Child Protection and Law Number 23 Year 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence, the Regional Government together with the community is obligated to undertake prevention, protection, and recovery efforts for victims of violence;
